(7108223, 1084031, 43463, '<td valign="top">Voted earlier coming back to comment.<br/> <br/>Nicely captured B&amp;W of the classic diner. And see what you did with the title!- Now I have the theme music from Guy Fieri''s show in my head :grumbles: need to find some other music to drive it out of my head. O.K. back to the photo:-) I like the angle and the B&amp;W treatment that gives plays into the feel of ''classic oldie''. I do have two suggestions on how to improve the visual impact more. First the contrast could be a little bit more dynamic. Playing with Levels to adjust highlights/midtones/shadows can increase the contrast and give it more pop. Second, is composition. You got the right angle you just needed to move the bar stools a little more to the right so that the line come out from the bottom right corner. That way it acts as a great leading line and draws the eye to explore the rest of the diner.</td>', 'Voted earlier coming back to comment. Nicely captured B&W of the classic diner. And see what you did with the title!- Now I have the theme music from Guy Fieri''s show in my head :grumbles: need to find some other music to drive it out of my head. O.K. back to the photo:-) I like the angle and the B&W treatment that gives plays into the feel of ''classic oldie''. I do have two suggestions on how to improve the visual impact more. First the contrast could be a little bit more dynamic. Playing with Levels to adjust highlights/midtones/shadows can increase the contrast and give it more pop. Second, is composition. You got the right angle you just needed to move the bar stools a little more to the right so that the line come out from the bottom right corner. That way it acts as a great leading line and draws the eye to explore the rest of the diner.', '2013-09-28 22:22:38.000000', NULL, 1),
(7108232, 1084115, 68503, '<td valign="top">Yeah this is bad ass!!! Great job on replicating the original and making it better.</td>', 'Yeah this is bad ass!!! Great job on replicating the original and making it better.', '2013-09-28 22:51:35.000000', NULL, 1),
(7108235, 1084045, 68503, '<td valign="top">Great attempt on trying to replicate the original. Colors are much better in this version.</td>', 'Great attempt on trying to replicate the original. Colors are much better in this version.', '2013-09-28 22:53:42.000000', NULL, 1),
(7108238, 1084132, 43463, '<td valign="top">Voted earlier coming back to comment.<br/> <br/>While it doesn''t have the sense of movement of the original what it does have is a stunning view of the mountain scenery beauty that this train is traveling through. Great details in this shot from the tracks, to the foliage to the engine. Love that you composed the angle so that the train and tracks are traveling to the right bottom corner - leading lines that draw the eye to the main subject and the lovely scenery in the backdrop. The processing really brought the yellow and red tones but I feel it is a bit too saturated. The yellow of the train and the is a bit too overpowering especially with all the golden foliage around it. The rail on the tracks has a red that is almost glowing. Not sure the color of the sky works - it has an ominous mood to it which doesn''t pair well with the beautiful tranquil scenery.</td>', 'Voted earlier coming back to comment. While it doesn''t have the sense of movement of the original what it does have is a stunning view of the mountain scenery beauty that this train is traveling through. Great details in this shot from the tracks, to the foliage to the engine. Love that you composed the angle so that the train and tracks are traveling to the right bottom corner - leading lines that draw the eye to the main subject and the lovely scenery in the backdrop. The processing really brought the yellow and red tones but I feel it is a bit too saturated. The yellow of the train and the is a bit too overpowering especially with all the golden foliage around it. The rail on the tracks has a red that is almost glowing. Not sure the color of the sky works - it has an ominous mood to it which doesn''t pair well with the beautiful tranquil scenery.', '2013-09-28 23:06:18.000000', NULL, 1),
(7108245, 1083648, 43463, '<td valign="top">Voted earlier coming back to vote.<br/> <br/>The light is lit!!! Different bulb than the original but I think in this redux it is better because it fills out the frame more. Overall the photo is a bit dark which does help make the lightbulb pop more off the background, but the drawback is that the outlet is too much in the shadows that it gets lost. I think that this would be better if the exposure was a bit brighter either through slower shutter speed paired with lower aperture to let more light in or perhaps in PP with Levels and Curves.</td>', 'Voted earlier coming back to vote. The light is lit!!! Different bulb than the original but I think in this redux it is better because it fills out the frame more. Overall the photo is a bit dark which does help make the lightbulb pop more off the background, but the drawback is that the outlet is too much in the shadows that it gets lost. I think that this would be better if the exposure was a bit brighter either through slower shutter speed paired with lower aperture to let more light in or perhaps in PP with Levels and Curves.', '2013-09-28 23:22:12.000000', NULL, 1),
(7108247, 1083630, 43463, '<td valign="top">Voted earlier coming back to comment and after pondering upon it a bump up.<br/> <br/>Whoa! This has the water bottle from the original and a whole lot more. Reading the MSmidt23 photographer''s comments I took what the original artist intended to show in the shot but didn''t. "Water bottles are the most common plastic object used today and if we keep this rate up our earth will lose all its beauty and no amazing photos will be taken anymore." You set out to show that plastic is indeed everywhere from the water bottles on the left to the eyeglass frames, possibly the dress, the bike helmet with the crazy headdress adornments, etc. etc. etc. The plastic of the bottles and elsewhere clutters up the frame and maybe that is what you were aiming to show your audience. Natural beauty overrun and spoiled by non biodegradable plastics/litter.</td>', 'Voted earlier coming back to comment and after pondering upon it a bump up. Whoa! This has the water bottle from the original and a whole lot more. Reading the MSmidt23 photographer''s comments I took what the original artist intended to show in the shot but didn''t. "Water bottles are the most common plastic object used today and if we keep this rate up our earth will lose all its beauty and no amazing photos will be taken anymore." You set out to show that plastic is indeed everywhere from the water bottles on the left to the eyeglass frames, possibly the dress, the bike helmet with the crazy headdress adornments, etc. etc. etc. The plastic of the bottles and elsewhere clutters up the frame and maybe that is what you were aiming to show your audience. Natural beauty overrun and spoiled by non biodegradable plastics/litter.', '2013-09-28 23:32:08.000000', NULL, 1),
