(7109341, 1084044, 43463, '<td valign="top">Voted earlier coming back to comment.<br/> <br/>Hmmm, the General''s hidden DQ from the Games Challenge;-). <br/> <br/>It remains true to the original with the "Keep off the Grass" sign. This redux has a leading line in it that the original did not feature prominently. The only thing is, is that dirt path/line doesn''t really lead the eye to any element that would help the composition or play into/support the main subject. Maybe if the composition showed the corner where that path ends and a person (someone dressed in baseball outfit would be best given the location) walking towards it. Then that leading line would have something the eye could focus on and it would be another supporting element that would be a nod back to the ''keep off the grass'' sign.</td>', 'Voted earlier coming back to comment. Hmmm, the General''s hidden DQ from the Games Challenge;-).  It remains true to the original with the "Keep off the Grass" sign. This redux has a leading line in it that the original did not feature prominently. The only thing is, is that dirt path/line doesn''t really lead the eye to any element that would help the composition or play into/support the main subject. Maybe if the composition showed the corner where that path ends and a person (someone dressed in baseball outfit would be best given the location) walking towards it. Then that leading line would have something the eye could focus on and it would be another supporting element that would be a nod back to the ''keep off the grass'' sign.', '2013-10-01 17:09:34.000000', NULL, 1),
(7109348, 1083470, 43463, '<td valign="top">Voted earlier coming back to comment.<br/> <br/>What a cool find of this pattern of a woman on eroding wall! The addition of the lips further helps bring the imagery of this woman to the forefront - the pose takes on the look of a pouting model on a fashion magazine. One critique I have is that the lips don''t look properly registered to the ''ground'' and the tones don''t quite match the tones of the rest of the photo composition. There is a shadow edge on the bottom right that makes it look pasted on - which it might have been in either PP or physically on the wall:-) As for the tones on the lips they look washed out either because it was a seperate shot where the lighting was different than the one for the wall or it was actually on the wall but the lighting was reflected stronger on the glossy surface. A quick pass with levels and curves could correct the tones for this surreal lady to shine.</td>', 'Voted earlier coming back to comment. What a cool find of this pattern of a woman on eroding wall! The addition of the lips further helps bring the imagery of this woman to the forefront - the pose takes on the look of a pouting model on a fashion magazine. One critique I have is that the lips don''t look properly registered to the ''ground'' and the tones don''t quite match the tones of the rest of the photo composition. There is a shadow edge on the bottom right that makes it look pasted on - which it might have been in either PP or physically on the wall:-) As for the tones on the lips they look washed out either because it was a seperate shot where the lighting was different than the one for the wall or it was actually on the wall but the lighting was reflected stronger on the glossy surface. A quick pass with levels and curves could correct the tones for this surreal lady to shine.', '2013-10-01 17:26:34.000000', NULL, 1),
